<b>Kushiro</b>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>Memanbetsu</b>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>Hakodate</b>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>Tokachi-Obihiro</b>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>Aomori</b>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>Komatsu</b>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>Flight No.</b>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>First Class</b>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>J Class</b>

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:15.930
<b>Coach</b>

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:16.930
Here.

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:20.440
Oh... thanks.

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:24.350
Seriously though, did it not occur 
to you to message me on LINE?

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:26.700
Or just call me, maybe?

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:28.930
Sorry.

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:31.560
Obviously I'm not quitting.

00:15:31.560 --> 00:15:34.280
After you managed to pull 
my team out of a fire...

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:38.450
How pathetic would I be if I ran off 
before I could pay you back?

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.970
Uh... what about Okinawa?

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:42.750
I've changed my mind.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.950
I canceled the flight, 
so don't worry about it.

00:15:45.370 --> 00:15:46.150
Sorry.

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:47.760
You don't have to apologize.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:48.960
Oh... sorry.

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:58.580
Why were you so worried about me, anyway?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:03.090
Well... I was scared.

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:09.140
Everyone else left... 
I was afraid you would go, too.

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:10.490
Hashiba...

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:15.550
Shinoaki... Tsurayuki... 
They were both so amazing.

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:19.900
But before I realized it, 
both had given up on being creators.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:21.500
Even Nanako...

00:16:22.070 --> 00:16:25.000
It's all my fault.

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:30.960
I think I'm trying to help people, 
but in the end, all I do is help myself.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:33.800
The things I do to try and help others...

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:37.330
just end up making them miserable.

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:38.630
I see.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:41.650
You've been saying that this entire time...

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:43.760
About how you feel guilty 
about what happened.

00:16:43.760 --> 00:16:45.840
About how you're worthless.

00:16:46.670 --> 00:16:50.860
And whenever I asked you about it, 
you would just clam up.

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:54.270
It's the truth.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:02.220
You think they're all miserable 
because of you.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:04.260
You really do, don't you?

00:17:04.260 --> 00:17:08.710
Yeah. I should've never 
been here in the first place.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.140
I see.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:22.640
Kawasegawa?

00:17:28.810 --> 00:17:30.230
What was that for?!

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:31.520
Shut up!

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.820
God, you are so annoying!

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:37.180
C-Cut it out! What did I say?!

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:38.710
You didn't <i>say</i> anything!

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:43.270
You were always an honor student, 
and such a straight shooter,

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:45.710
enough that you made me feel jealous!

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:47.510
K-Kawasegawa?

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:51.120
So, why?! Why did you never ask for help?!

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:54.070
Why do you always try 
to handle everything yourself?!

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:57.020
Did you think we couldn't handle it?

00:17:57.020 --> 00:18:01.410
Why didn't you try leaning on someone else 
when you didn't know what to do?!

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:08.660
You weren't able to support 
yourself after awhile.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:10.390
It's the same as before.

00:18:11.030 --> 00:18:14.400
You were chasing after 
Tsurayuki after he left,

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:17.230
trying to write scripts even 
though it wasn't your thing...

00:18:17.940 --> 00:18:21.370
It never occurred to you 
to find another writer.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.370
You didn't put up any resistance 
when Shinoaki decided to stop drawing,

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:27.710
and couldn't help Nanako 
through her frustration.

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:31.210
But... But...

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:34.340
How does that amount to being 
responsible for their futures?!

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:37.040
Who says that's your responsibility?!

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:39.680
It's not like you made them do anything!

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:42.880
Why would you blame yourself?!

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:45.640
To the point of depression 
and getting so torn up...

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:48.140
"I'm useless."

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:51.900
How could... How could you possibly think that?!

00:18:55.430 --> 00:19:00.410
You've always, always worked so hard.

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:06.180
You always put your personal stuff aside, 
and always try to help other people,

00:19:06.180 --> 00:19:09.160
so they'd be able to make something.

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:12.440
When we laughed, we all laughed together,

00:19:12.440 --> 00:19:14.620
but when you cried, 
you always did it alone.

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:19.420
You haven't done a single thing wrong.

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:22.540
And if anyone says otherwise,

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:26.010
I won't let them get away with it!

00:19:26.390 --> 00:19:27.930
You understand me?!

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.740
So have a little confidence!

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:35.150
You should've never been here?! 
There's no way that's true!

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:41.590
Or would you say you being around 
to save me was a mistake, too?!

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:43.590
Am I right?!

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:47.330
You're amazing, okay?! I promise!

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:50.130
Out of everyone I've ever met...

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:54.340
You're the most generous, 
most exciting, hardest to predict...

00:19:54.770 --> 00:19:57.700
And that's why I loved you! 
Why I looked up to you!

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:00.470
So stop being so pessimistic!

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:12.730
U-Um... did you just...

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:16.100
Forget those last two. Too much information.

00:20:16.100 --> 00:20:17.930
O-Okay...

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.900
Um... sorry—

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:26.040
I mean... uh...

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:29.490
Thank you, Kawasegawa.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.520
Lukewarm.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.520
Lukewarm.

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.930
Listen... hypothetically...

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:05.780
If I found myself back in time, 
in front of you, when you were suffering...

00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:07.910
I think I would've done 
whatever it took to help you.

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:11.370
But knowing how you were back then,

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:14.800
you would've never actually 
turned to me for help.

00:21:15.160 --> 00:21:19.300
No... You've helped me 
a lot already, Kawasegawa.

00:21:19.640 --> 00:21:20.960
More than enough.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.380
Except I didn't.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:26.010
Listen, I have no idea if there's such 
a thing as reincarnation,

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:29.550
but next time? I'm going to 
actually help you.

00:21:29.550 --> 00:21:30.720
Got it?

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:36.440
Okay. I'll be counting on you, then.

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:50.950
Okay! I think I'm going to 
Okinawa after all.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:55.000
I'll see if I can exchange my ticket,

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:57.830
and if I can, I'll catch the next flight.

00:22:01.390 --> 00:22:04.700
Don't worry. I'm coming back.

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:05.800
See ya.

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:07.150
Kawasegawa!

00:22:07.150 --> 00:22:08.640
One other thing...

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:12.660
You blame yourself for everybody quitting,

00:22:12.660 --> 00:22:15.640
but you managed to help 
one person, at least.

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:16.820
I did?

00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:18.390
I mean Minori Ayaka.

00:22:18.390 --> 00:22:23.330
The game that you made 
is what got her drawing, right?

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:28.290
Yeah. I guess I did help someone, at least.

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:30.280
In this world...

00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:35.840
Everything has some purpose, I think.

00:22:46.680 --> 00:22:51.320
<i>She really did save me.</i>

00:23:02.380 --> 00:23:05.070
I wish I could go back to the old days.

00:23:05.070 --> 00:23:07.800
Yeah, I figured it was about time for that.

00:23:12.980 --> 00:23:16.410
Yo, Hashiba-kun. How you been?

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:18.220
It's you...

00:23:31.650 --> 00:23:34.480
Hello again, Keiko-san.
